  * Lazily created on first use rather than in RtlInitializeCriticalSection,
  * because a title can perfectly well use a statically zeroed one it never
  * announced.
+ *
+ * Xbox has no RtlDeleteCriticalSection. Titles that put locks inside heap
+ * objects therefore abandon shadow entries whenever those objects are freed at
+ * a new address. A fixed open-address table that never reclaims fills up, after
+ * which Enter becomes a no-op and the title races into a hang -- MvC2 does this
+ * after a few fights. Slots carry a refcount spanning Enter..Leave so idle
+ * abandoned entries can be deleted under the table lock without pulling a host
+ * CRITICAL_SECTION out from under a thread already on its way into it.
+ * Tombstones keep open-address probe chains intact across reclaim.
